ntil November 2 at 7:30PM MST by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"Upstream flooding along the Rio Grande continues downstream near\nMonte Vista in Rio Grande County.\n\n* WHAT...Flooding along the Rio Grande near Monte Vista is forecasted\nto begin by late morning on Monday.\n\n* WHERE...East Central Rio Grande County in south central Colorado...\nWest Central Alamosa County in southeastern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 730 PM MST Monday.\n\n* IMPACTS...The Rio Grande continues to rise due to upstream flooding\nthrough Del Norte and South Fork. Extensive inundation of low-lying\nareas adjacent to the river is expected. Inundation of low spots\nalong Highway 185, some homes, and other structures may be possible\nfor areas south of the river. Expect many areas of slow moving or\nstanding water.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 717 PM MST, Upstream stream gauges on the Rio Grande and South\nFork Rio Grande indicate that flooding is occurring.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nMonte Vista.\n- http://water.noaa.gov","ends":"2026-11-02T19:30:00-07:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Alamosa, CO; Rio Grande, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.8381198fb91f2cdc89afc94409f49a58e0647b23.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.8381198fb91f2cdc89afc94409f49a58e0647b23.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued November 1 at 7:09PM MST until November 6 at 1:00AM MST by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"...The Flood Watch continues for the following rivers in Colorado...\n\nRio Grande At Alamosa affecting Alamosa Vicinity/Central San Luis\nValley.\n\nFor the Rio Grande...including Alamosa...flooding is forecasted to\nbegin by mid week.\n\n* WHAT...Flooding along the Rio Grande through Alamosa is forecasted\nto begin by mid week.\n\n* WHERE...Rio Grande at Alamosa.\n\n* WHEN...From Wednesday morning to late Thursday night.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 6:30 PM MST Sunday the stage was 3.0 feet.\n- Forecast...Flood s